time to get  cooking with nanny bubbe today she is  showing us how to make  a delicious beet salad welcome back  nanny bubbe i cannot wait to hear this  it sounds perfect for the summer time  doesn't it really but i've got it i've  got to tell you there's  tremendous feedback right now anyway  there is  um it is very i'm so sorry i'm hearing  myself come back into my own ears and  i'm losing my thoughts so i apologize  so let me just tell you that uh i had a  beet salad  in laguna beach and it was absolutely  amazing  and i absolutely wanted to do it but  beets seem so daunting to me they seem  like ecommerce  and it seems like you can actually like  cutting through the skin or cutting  through the meat is very very difficult  but i found out after this salad it was  so delicious  i really worked hard to figure out a  great recipe  and so here it is so the first thing i  want to tell you is to separate your red  beets from your golden beets it's very  important  and what i'm going to show you is as you  cut it off it starts bleeding  all over everything so you always want a  piece put a piece of parchment  underneath it  and you always want to do your golden  beets before your red beets  and because if you don't see what  happens you will get your golden beets  pink  so we're going to slice off the ends we  are going  to shave off the skin and one of the  most important things to tell you  is that if you put the entire bulb  into the pot to steam it will  automatically  make the outer part of the bulb very  very overdone and the inner part under  done  so you really want to dice it and or  slice it before you put it into the  steaming pot  and so i'm just going to show you really  quickly that we're going to dice it  whoop  dicing it here slicing and then some  dicing real fast  and into the pot into the silicone  steaming basket so i'll just take a  handful  and just show you it goes right in like  that  and then each piece will be perfectly  perfectly steamed  so 